<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bowdoin College</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bowdoin College is a private liberal arts college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, Maine, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, founded in 1794. Its graduates include the writer Nathaniel Hawthorne, the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-wadsworth-longfellow">Henry Wadsworth Longfellow</a> and President Franklin Pierce. In 1826 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-brown-russwurm">John Brown Russwurm</a> became its first African American graduate, one of the first Black graduates of any American college.</p></div>
